# Architecture

## Control plane

This repository owns program gates, interface approval, compatibility records,
immutable registries, and cross-repository dependency state. It contains no
scientific implementation and never launches a producer or consumer pipeline.

## Compute repositories

Producer repositories own acquired-input metadata, manifests, preprocessing,
representation code/training, telemetry, checkpoints, exports, and producer
jobs. Consumer repositories own ingestion, scientific measures, null models,
validation, statistics, figures, reporting, and consumer jobs.

An implementation task remains in its owning repository. A program Bead links
the local task only when coordination, a gate, or another repository depends on
it.

## Interface boundary

The public producer hosts the canonical data-interface schema and valid/invalid
fixtures so its CI never depends on a private control repository. Consumers pin
the producer contract commit and schema digest. This repository registers the
approved producer revision, consumer revision, schema hash, and conformance
result.

Artifacts cross the boundary through durable URIs plus full SHA-256 identities.
They never cross through sibling imports, unregistered workstation paths, Git
submodules, copied source trees, or payloads committed here.

## Trust boundaries

- `.beads/issues.jsonl` is mutable operational coordination state.
- ADRs are append-only human-accepted decisions.
- Registry drafts are reviewable; registered records are immutable.
- Schemas are immutable within a released version directory.
- Source repositories and artifact stores remain authoritative for code and
  payload bytes.
